purpose: Paradigm Conductor — workspace manager + multimodal mission control for Claude Code sessions + Symphony inter-agent messaging
version: 0.16.0
description: "Workspace manager that launches and owns CC instances. Session manager with recent project persistence, checkpoint reading, and headless agent spawning. Shared camera architecture — single AVCaptureSession feeds both gaze and gesture Vision providers simultaneously. Video/voice toggle controls with keyboard shortcuts. Eyebrow-triggered voice control, custom gesture recording, voice command binding, gaze-to-grid zone targeting, and Paradigm context enrichment. Targeted terminal close (per-window, not kill-all). Native macOS Swift/SwiftUI app launched via paradigm conductor CLI command. Single-owner architecture — AppDelegate owns orchestrator, workspace, project store, and agent process manager lifecycle. Symphony Phase 1-2: auto-detects CC sessions, registers agent parts in The Score (~/.paradigm/score/), relays notes on 5s poll, file approval with trust config, thread list view, file request notification, and Symphony settings tab."
context:
  - Native macOS Swift/SwiftUI app
  - Ships via paradigm conductor CLI command
  - 7 platform abstraction protocols for future Windows port
  - All ML inference runs locally — zero cloud, zero cost, no Python dependency
  - SharedCameraSession distributes frames to gaze + gesture providers simultaneously
  - VisionGazeProvider uses VNDetectFaceLandmarksRequest for native gaze + eyebrow tracking
  - Sidebar-based workspace manager replaces floating overlay
  - Custom gesture recording via DTW matching
  - Voice command phrase binding with fuzzy matching
  - Single-owner pattern — AppDelegate is the sole lifecycle owner of orchestrator and workspace
  - Video/voice toggle icons in header bar with Cmd+Shift+V / Cmd+Shift+M hotkeys
  - Targeted terminal close via AppleScript window IDs — closing one window no longer kills all terminals
  - Symphony: file-based inter-agent messaging at ~/.paradigm/score/ with JSONL mailboxes
  - Symphony: auto-link creates agent parts when CC sessions are detected
  - Symphony: 5s relay poll routes notes between agent inboxes/outboxes
  - Symphony: file approval with trust.yaml, hard-deny patterns, SHA-256 hashing
  - Sprint 8: Session manager with recent projects, checkpoint reading, headless agent spawning via Process API
  - Sprint 8: ProjectStore persists to ~/.paradigm/conductor/recent-projects.json (survives reinstall)
  - Sprint 8: CheckpointReader reads .paradigm/session-checkpoint.json (wire-compat with paradigm-mcp SessionCheckpoint)
  - Sprint 8: AgentProcessManager spawns claude as child process with stdin/stdout piping
  - Sprint 9: Agent groups with cross-project membership, drag-and-drop reordering
  - Sprint 9: SymphonyMonitor polls inboxes for unread counts, threads, and last activity
  - Sprint 9: AgentNetworkView as primary orchestration dashboard with group panels
  - Sprint 9: ThreadView chat-like thread viewer with message compose (Maestro sends as human)
  - Sprint 10: Task protocol — 7 new intents (task, task-ack, progress, approval-request/response, task-complete/failed)
  - Sprint 10: TaskComposerView for structured task assignment to agents/groups
  - Sprint 10: ApprovalView + ApprovalNotificationBanner for approval-request gating
  - Sprint 10: task-protocol.ts agent-side prompt generation for received tasks
  - Sprint 11: TaskStore persists to ~/.paradigm/conductor/tasks.json, SymphonyMonitor routes task-intent notes
  - Sprint 11: TaskDashboardView (kanban columns) + TaskDetailView (timeline, files, symbols, blockers)
  - Sprint 12: AgentHealthMonitor computes per-agent success rate, avg time, sparklines from TaskStore
  - Sprint 12: SentinelLiveView (real-time event viewer) + AgentHealthView (health dashboard) + Monitoring settings tab
  - Sprint 12: SentinelWSClient buffers last 200 events with level field and Identifiable conformance
  - Sprint 13: EyebrowBindingRegistry — user-customizable eyebrow→action with state machine bypass
  - Sprint 13: HotKeyBindingRegistry + HotKeyRecorder — user-customizable hotkey→action with live Combine observation
  - Sprint 13: BindingsManagerView fully wired with 5 sections (gestures, voice, built-in, eyebrow, hotkeys)
  - Sprint 14: Task lifecycle completion — cancel, re-assign, archive. TaskArchive JSONL at ~/.paradigm/conductor/tasks-archive.jsonl
  - Sprint 14: TaskDetailView gains Cancel, Re-assign, View Thread action buttons with confirmation dialogs
  - Sprint 14: TaskDashboardView gains archive badge + menu (Archive Older than 7d, Archive All Completed)
  - Sprint 15: SentinelWSClient gains metadata parsing, activeSymbols tracking (frequency-sorted), symbol filter, clear buffer
  - Sprint 15: SentinelEventDetailView popover — full timestamp, level/type badges, metadata key-value, related tasks
  - Sprint 15: SentinelSymbolFilterView — horizontal chip bar for top 10 symbols with toggle selection
  - Sprint 15: SentinelLiveView enhanced — symbol filter, clickable symbols, event detail popover, clear button, filtered/total counts
  - Sprint 16: BindingsManagerView decomposed into 6 sub-views in UI/Views/Bindings/ (~30 lines vs 302)
  - Sprint 16: MainOverlayView mainContent decomposed into 12 named computed properties
  - Sprint 17: Container Window mode — full-screen NSWindow workspace with binary split tiling engine
  - Sprint 17: TilingEngine (recursive TileNode tree), 6 layout presets, cell split/remove/swap operations
  - Sprint 17: ContainerView with header, tiling area, status bar. CellChromeView with status badges + actions
  - Sprint 17: Menu bar switch between sidebar mode and container mode
  - Sprint 18: DividerHandle (drag-to-resize with snap at 25/33/50/67/75%), LayoutPresetsView (mini layout icons)
  - Sprint 18: CellActionMenu (split/maximize/close context menu), EmptyCellView (launch placeholder)
  - Sprint 18: ContainerView gains divider handles, animated layout transitions, maximize/restore toggle

